sers/catethos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catethos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catethos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catethos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catethos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catethos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":1408,"digest":"sha256:d73b3d920c7e4856eb898c131cf2820c7d5614cbd53a980f8c50eec384fac573","download_count":1,"created_at":"2026-09-08T15:16:48Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T15:16:48Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/catethos/Aphid/releases/download/v0.1.1-dev/x86_64-linux-gnu-identity.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catethos/Aphid/tarball/v0.1.1-dev","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catethos/Aphid/zipball/v0.1.1-dev","body":"# Aphid 0.1.1-dev — stability and correctness\n\nExperimental prerelease containing five narrowly scoped LadybugDB fixes:\n\n- Align packed FLOAT/DOUBLE sort-key and graph-path identifier accesses.\n- Avoid overflowing intermediate INT128 addition and negation operations.\n- Initialize ALTER defaults safely when an operator has no input result set.\n\nNew tests combine indexed transaction mutation with retained FTS, vector and\nDuckDB cursors across timeout, caller death, shutdown, index rebuild and persistent\nreopen. All 99 public tests pass on macOS against normal and fatal ASan/UBSan native\nbuilds. Both native Linux architectures also pass all 99 tests in source-build,\nrelocated-bundle and fresh compiler-free consumer runs. Final combined-package\nqualification is recorded in the release evidence. These are correctness/crash-safety fixes; no exploit or data\nexposure has been demonstrated.\n\nNative inputs are pinned by SHA256\n`09b8618810c5788237ebec1c8164c9322d0d65f4d312c41e4908687394647aba`.\nAll bundles for this release must be rebuilt from those inputs; the older\n`v0.1.0-dev` tag and assets remain unchanged.\n\nKeep each archive's `licenses/` directory and the accompanying\n`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` with redistributed native files. The supplement includes\nthe Zig MIT notice for the macOS bundle; the Hex installer places it in\napplication `priv/licenses/` automatically. `THIRD_PARTY.md` records the review\nboundaries.\n\nThis remains an experimental release, with no target declared release-supported.\nElixir 1.20.0 / OTP 29.0.4 is the qualified runtime. Minimum-system/CPU execution,\nbroader TSan and Zig allocation coverage, Linux sanitizers and the remaining\nimplementation-plan gates are not established by these host tests.\n"}